.TH CBMAP_DATA_NODE_DESTROY 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cbmap_data_node_destroy \- Destroy a CBMap data node

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB cbmap_data_node_destroy (struct cbmap_data_node* data, cbmap_allocator_t key_allocator, cbmap_allocator_t value_allocator);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcbmap_data_node_destroy\fR function is used to destroy a CBMap data node. This function releases the memory allocated for the node's key and value using the provided allocators.

The function takes three parameters:
.TP
.B data
A pointer to the CBMap data node to be destroyed.
.TP
.B key_allocator
A pointer to the allocator used for allocating memory for the node's key.
.TP
.B value_allocator
A pointer to the allocator used for allocating memory for the node's value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcbmap_data_node_destroy\fR function to destroy a CBMap data node:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>

int main() {
    struct cbmap_data_node node;
    cbmap_allocator_t key_allocator, value_allocator;

    // Initialize allocators
    key_allocator = ...;  // Initialize key allocator
    value_allocator = ...;  // Initialize value allocator

    // Assume node is initialized and used somewhere

    // Destroy the node
    cbmap_data_node_destroy(&node, key_allocator, value_allocator);

    return 0;
}
.nef